# An extension can't take the whiteboard away from unsaved work. tests/drive.rs installs the
# open-tasks example patched to open a note whenever the tasks change, which no extension
# should do unasked. While a card is being typed, and while the shape editor holds an unsaved
# draft, a task another program writes makes it ask: the card and the draft stay in front, the
# count still follows, and the editor's status line says what was not done. The card then
# saves with Esc and the shape with ctrl+s. tests/drive.rs reads both files after.
size 140x44
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 16 open tasks
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter · ⏎ open · Esc back
type Drafts
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Drafts · 0 cards
keys n
wait-for editing · type text · ⏎ new line · Esc done (saves)
type Draft
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
expect whiteboard Drafts
expect Draft▏
type , kept
wait-for Draft, kept▏
keys esc
wait-for whiteboard Drafts · 1 cards
# The shape editor with a triangle drawn and not saved.
keys S
wait-for shape editor · type to filter
keys enter
wait-for shape editor · shape1 (new) · vertices
click 10 34
click 10 64
click 23 79
click 10 34
wait-for closed path of 3 vertices
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n- [ ] Count the masks\n
wait-for ☐ 18 open tasks
wait-for open-tasks wanted to open Volcanoes/Krakatoa.md: not while the shape editor has unsaved changes
expect shape editor · shape1 (new)
expect path1: path, 3 vertices, closed
keys ctrl+s
wait-for saved shape1 in .cold-lava/shapes.toml
keys q
wait-for whiteboard Drafts · 1 cards
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
